    ],
    "tipsMd": "## Adjectives agree\n\nAn adjective changes its ending to match the noun it describes: **-o** for a masculine noun like **hermano**, **-a** for a feminine noun like **hermana** or **familia**.\n\n- **alto** and **alta** mean tall\n- **bajo** and **baja** mean short\n- **simpático** and **simpática** mean nice\n\n> Mi hermano es **alto**. Mi hermana es **alta**.\n\nSome adjectives, like **joven**, are the same for men and women. For two or more people, add **-s** or **-es**: **altos**, **jóvenes**.\n\n## Mi, tu and tú\n\n**Mi** means my and **tu** means your. With an accent, **tú** means you."
  },
